<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Definitions_Process_Finance" targetNamespace="http://corso-processi.local/apqc">
  <bpmn:process id="Process_Finance" name="9.2.2 Invoice customer" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Category 9.0 Manage Financial Resources
Process Group 9.2 Perform revenue accounting (10729)
Process 9.2.2 Invoice customer (10743)

Definizione APQC: Preparing detailed reports of customer purchases. Prepare a commercial document between the seller and customer with details about transaction. Detail the quantity purchased, price of products/services, date, parties involved, unique invoice number, and tax information.

Fonte: APQC PCF Cross-Industry v8.0 — Definitions and Key Measures, Category 9.0 Manage Financial Resources (K012582).

Documentazione completa del processo (SIPOC, matrice variabili, scheda sintetica): esempi-apqc/07-finance/processo.md
Framework: APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF) Cross-Industry v8.0 — https://www.apqc.org/process-frameworks</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_1">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Bill" name="Billing Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>T1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>T2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>T3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_AR" name="Accounts Receivable">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>T4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>T5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start" name="Ordine evaso / servizio erogato">

      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:task id="T1" name="9.2.2.1 Maintain customer/product master files (10794)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Definizione APQC: Creating and updating a record of customers and the products being purchased by them in a database. Such a master-file can be used to ensure customer touch point, enhance customer satisfaction, explore cross selling opportunities, and identify future trends.

Fonte: APQC PCF Cross-Industry v8.0 — Definitions and Key Measures, Category 9.0 Manage Financial Resources (K012582).

Documentazione completa del processo (SIPOC, matrice variabili, scheda sintetica): esempi-apqc/07-finance/processo.md
Framework: APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF) Cross-Industry v8.0 — https://www.apqc.org/process-frameworks</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="T2" name="9.2.2.2 Generate customer billing data (10795)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Definizione APQC: Preparing detailed reports about products purchased by customers. Record and generate a detailed account of transactions made by customers at a particular time and location. Include all details about products such as price, quantity, and name.

Fonte: APQC PCF Cross-Industry v8.0 — Definitions and Key Measures, Category 9.0 Manage Financial Resources (K012582).

Documentazione completa del processo (SIPOC, matrice variabili, scheda sintetica): esempi-apqc/07-finance/processo.md
Framework: APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF) Cross-Industry v8.0 — https://www.apqc.org/process-frameworks</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="T3" name="9.2.2.3 Transmit billing data to customers (10796)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Definizione APQC: Providing information to customers about purchases made by them. Communicate the details of purchases. Provide customers with a copy of details for their reference.

Fonte: APQC PCF Cross-Industry v8.0 — Definitions and Key Measures, Category 9.0 Manage Financial Resources (K012582).

Documentazione completa del processo (SIPOC, matrice variabili, scheda sintetica): esempi-apqc/07-finance/processo.md
Framework: APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF) Cross-Industry v8.0 — https://www.apqc.org/process-frameworks</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="T4" name="9.2.2.4 Post receivable entries (10797)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Definizione APQC: Registering transactions and their scheduled payments.

Fonte: APQC PCF Cross-Industry v8.0 — Definitions and Key Measures, Category 9.0 Manage Financial Resources (K012582).

Documentazione completa del processo (SIPOC, matrice variabili, scheda sintetica): esempi-apqc/07-finance/processo.md
Framework: APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF) Cross-Industry v8.0 — https://www.apqc.org/process-frameworks</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="T5" name="9.2.2.5 Resolve customer billing inquiries (10798)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Definizione APQC: Checking and solving billing queries raised by customers.

Fonte: APQC PCF Cross-Industry v8.0 — Definitions and Key Measures, Category 9.0 Manage Financial Resources (K012582).

Documentazione completa del processo (SIPOC, matrice variabili, scheda sintetica): esempi-apqc/07-finance/processo.md
Framework: APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF) Cross-Industry v8.0 — https://www.apqc.org/process-frameworks</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End" name="Fattura registrata in AR">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_6</bpmn:incoming>

    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1" sourceRef="Start" targetRef="T1" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_2" sourceRef="T1" targetRef="T2" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_3" sourceRef="T2" targetRef="T3" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_4" sourceRef="T3" targetRef="T4" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_5" sourceRef="T4" targetRef="T5" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_6" sourceRef="T5" targetRef="End" />
  </bpmn:process>
